# Root certificates of the two free public time-stamp services GrowSigning is set up to use.
# TSA_TRUST=bundled reads this list (a copy of it is built into src/server/tsaroots.ts, and
# tests/seal-csc.test.ts checks that the two are the same and that the fingerprints below hold).
#
# Downloaded on 2026-11-23 and checked against the SHA-256 fingerprints each authority publishes:
#
# 1. DigiCert Trusted Root G4 (used by http://timestamp.digicert.com)
#    from https://cacerts.digicert.com/DigiCertTrustedRootG4.crt
#    SHA-256 55:2F:7B:DC:F1:A7:AF:9E:6C:E6:72:01:7F:4F:12:AB:F7:72:40:C7:8E:76:1A:C2:03:D1:D9:D2:0A:C8:99:88
#    published at https://www.digicert.com/kb/digicert-root-certificates.htm
#
# 2. DigiCert Assured ID Root CA (DigiCert's service also sends a copy of Trusted Root G4 issued by this root)
#    from https://cacerts.digicert.com/DigiCertAssuredIDRootCA.crt
#    SHA-256 3E:90:99:B5:01:5E:8F:48:6C:00:BC:EA:9D:11:1E:E7:21:FA:BA:35:5A:89:BC:F1:DF:69:56:1E:3D:C6:32:5C
#    published at https://www.digicert.com/kb/digicert-root-certificates.htm
#
# 3. SSL.com Root Certification Authority RSA (used by http://ts.ssl.com)
#    from https://www.ssl.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/02/SSLcom-RootCAs.zip (SSLcomRootCertificationAuthorityRSA.pem)
#    SHA-256 85:66:6A:56:2E:E0:BE:5C:E9:25:C1:D8:89:0A:6F:76:A8:7E:C1:6D:4D:7D:5F:29:EA:74:19:CF:20:12:3B:69
#    published at https://www.ssl.com/repository/
#
# Check it yourself: openssl x509 -in <one block> -noout -fingerprint -sha256

